course: dictionary
lesson: 12938
title: Exactitude: being exact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exactitude is a formal word for being completely exact, correct and careful about small details. Its root word is exact, so think of exactitude as exactness. «The scientist measured the liquid with exactitude, so every test was fair.» The clues are measured and fair: the scientist was careful about every small amount.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The detective checked every clue with exactitude.» A detective who checks every clue is careful and does not miss small details. Try your meaning in the sentence: "checked every clue with great care and correctness" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Exactitude is a noun for a quality, so you can say «the exactitude of the map». It is uncountable, so do not add an s. It is used in formal writing and in careful work like science, maths and measuring.
fact: Exactitude means being completely exact, correct and careful about small details.
fact: The root word is exact, which means correct and precise.
fact: Exactitude is a formal word, so it is used more in writing and careful work than in everyday chat.
fact: «She measured the flour with exactitude.» means she measured it very carefully and correctly.
fact: Exactitude is uncountable: you say «great exactitude», not «exactitudes».
exercise: «The watchmaker fixed the tiny gears with exactitude.» What does exactitude mean here? | *Great care and correctness about small details | Being bored with the task | Speed and rushing | Loud noise
exercise: Which word is the root of exactitude? | excite | exit | exam | *exact
exercise: Ben says exactitude is just a fancy way to say fast. Why is he wrong? | Exactitude means loud | *Exactitude means care and correctness, not speed | Exactitude means fast, so he is right | Exactitude means happy
test: «The chef followed the recipe with exactitude, weighing every egg.» What does exactitude suggest about the chef? | Hungry | Lazy and messy | *Careful and correct | Tired of cooking
test: Which sentence uses exactitude correctly? | Exactitude sang a song to the class. | She ran exactitude across the field. | The exactitudes were loud in the hall. | *The pilot checked the route with exactitude.
exam: Which phrase best matches «scientific exactitude»? | Loud singing in a school hall | Quick, rough guesses | *Careful, precise work in science | A long summer holiday
